From e944a7774134a3f65d1699529ed75554f6b5f3de Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jernej Skrabec <jernej.skrabec@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 22:01:44 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 502/509] ASoC: sun4i-i2s: add HDMI IEC958 transport

Detect hdmi-codec from the already constructed ASoC runtime at DAI
startup. Expose IEC958_SUBFRAME_LE only when that runtime contains
hdmi-codec, and constrain the format out on every other link.

Install paired format and access rules on HDMI runtimes so mmap cannot
bypass the dmaengine PCM process callback. Translate canonical ALSA
IEC958 subframes in place after the userspace copy, moving the 16-bit
payload and PCUV bits into the Synopsys BPCUV representation and deriving
B from the Z preamble.

For controller layouts with multiple transmit data lines, distribute
HDMI channels over up to four lines and restore the line configuration
after runtime resume. Ordinary PCM remains unchanged.

Signed-off-by: Jernej Skrabec <jernej.skrabec@gmail.com>
